.DS_Store

# scripts/sync-assets.js needs Firebase Admin SDK access — unlike
# firebase-config.js (the public web client config, safe to commit),
# a service account key grants full read/write bypassing every
# firestore.rules check and must never be committed. See README's
# "3D model integration" section for how to get one.
node_modules/
serviceAccountKey.json
*.serviceaccount.json

# The model's export — hotel layout/room data, never committed to this
# public repo (see CLAUDE.md). Passed to scripts/sync-assets.js locally
# only.
assets.json

# Tracks the hash of the last assets.json actually synced to live/the
# emulator, so a rerun against an unchanged file can skip Firestore
# entirely. Per-machine state, not something to share via this repo.
.sync-assets-state.json

# Local Firebase emulator (dev/testing only — see README). Exported
# data is a local snapshot of test data, not something to share via
# this public repo; the debug logs are just noise.
emulator-data/
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log
database-debug.log
pubsub-debug.log
firebase-debug.log

# Shared dev backend (see README's "Shared dev backend" section) — the
# persistent emulator's data volume, the Cloudflare Tunnel's real config
# (has a credentials-file path and tunnel ID, generated per-machine by
# `cloudflared tunnel create`), and any job-sample export used to seed it.
# None of this is live data, a secret to hand out, or something to
# version — the .example file is the one that's committed.
docker/dev-emulator/data/
cloudflared/config.yml
cloudflared/*.json
jobs-sample.json
